<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=arch">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Building and engineering</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arch</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">before 3800 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">An arch is a curved structure spanning an opening, bearing the load above it or serving as decoration, first known in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/near-east">ancient Near East</a>, where the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nippur">Nippur</a> arch was built before 3800 BCE. There it was used rarely, mostly underground in structures such as drains, where sideways thrust is much reduced. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a>, who learned the semicircular arch from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/etruscans">Etruscans</a>, were the first builders in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> to use its full potential above ground, in bridges, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aqueduct">aqueducts</a> and the Colosseum. Wrought iron and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/steel">steel</a> reduced its structural role from the mid-19th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arch.jpg" alt="Arch" width="320" height="492" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Doulisath · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:02%CE%A3%CF%84%CE%AC%CE%B4%CE%B9%CE%BF_%CE%91%CF%81%CF%87%CE%B1%CE%AF%CE%B1%CF%82_%CE%9F%CE%BB%CF%85%CE%BC%CF%80%CE%AF%CE%B1%CF%8201.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>before 3800 BCE</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>Nippur, Mesopotamia</dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>H. V. Hilprecht dated the Nippur arch to before 4000 BCE.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/mudbrick">Mudbrick<span>c. 9000 BCE</span></a></div><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Led to</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/aqueduct">Aqueduct<span>c. 2000 BCE</span></a><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/anji-bridge">Segmental arch bridge<span>595–605</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=arch">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
